      "message": "\u003e Or do you mean that it will break because those older devices don\u0027t even support vm check-feature?\n\nYep. Essentially the vm check-feature is our way of answering the \"does this build have this trunk stable flag enabled?\" question. \n\nAlso, i think that isFeatureEnabled implementation (https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/android15-qpr1-release:packages/modules/Virtualization/tests/hostside/helper/java/com/android/microdroid/test/host/MicrodroidHostTestCaseBase.java;l\u003d246-250;drc\u003dfa6cc092912b0f886d156e614736111359f5ae62) has a bug - if you call it on older release that doesn\u0027t have check-feature-enabled command, it will fail with the error along the lines of \"no command check-feature-enabled\". The code will grep for the existence of the \"enabled\" in the output, and hapily tell you that feature is enabled :D",
